  "title": "Epiphenomenalism",
  "role": "model",
  "summary": "Epiphenomenalism, from Thomas Huxley's conscious automata of 1874 to Frank Jackson's epiphenomenal qualia of 1982: mental events are caused by events in the brain but have no effects on anything physical. Behavior has a complete physical cause, and conscious experience, a nonphysical property shown by the knowledge argument, accompanies it like a steam whistle on a locomotive.",
